{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 136, :comments ["<b>Streams</b> — connected to the matter of human oppression: they seek to oppress me, so that I not keep Your precepts, and I am anxious and weep over those who did not keep Your Torah — for I know that their end is evil. And some say: for they kept the way of parable upon the eyes, in the manner of: ואחרי עיניכם (\"after your eyes\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:51.867544964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}